2b) Implement different layout structures using row, column, stack widgets

// Import Flutter's Material Design library.
// It provides widgets such as Scaffold, AppBar, Text, Row, Column, etc.
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';


// The main() function is the starting point of the Dart program.
void main() {

  // runApp() starts the Flutter application.
  // MyApp is the root widget of our application.
  runApp(const MyApp());
}


// MyApp is a StatelessWidget.
// StatelessWidget means the widget's data does not change automatically.
class MyApp extends StatelessWidget {

  // Constructor of MyApp.
  const MyApp({super.key});


  // build() creates the user interface of MyApp.
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {

    // MaterialApp is the root widget of the Flutter application.
    return MaterialApp(

      // Removes the DEBUG banner from the top-right corner.
      debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false,

      // LayoutDemo is the first screen shown by the application.
      home: LayoutDemo(),
    );
  }
}


// LayoutDemo is another StatelessWidget.
class LayoutDemo extends StatelessWidget {

  // Constructor of LayoutDemo.
  const LayoutDemo({super.key});


  // Builds the user interface of LayoutDemo.
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {

    // Scaffold provides the basic screen structure.
    return Scaffold(

      // AppBar creates the top application bar.
      appBar: AppBar(

        // Displays the title in the AppBar.
        title: const Text("Row, Column & Stack Demo"),

        // Sets the AppBar background color to blue.
        backgroundColor: Colors.blue,
      ),


      // body contains the main content of the screen.
      body: SingleChildScrollView(

        // SingleChildScrollView allows the screen to scroll
        // when the content is larger than the screen.
        child: Padding(

          // Adds 16 pixels of space around the content.
          padding: const EdgeInsets.all(16.0),

          // Column arranges widgets vertically.
          child: Column(

            // Aligns the children toward the start (left side).
            crossAxisAlignment: CrossAxisAlignment.start,

            // Contains all the widgets inside the Column.
            children: [


              // ------------------------------------------------
              // ROW EXAMPLE
              // ------------------------------------------------

              // Displays the heading "1. Row Widget".
              const Text(
                "1. Row Widget",

                // Text formatting.
                style: TextStyle(
                  fontSize: 22,
                  fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                ),
              ),


              // Adds 10 pixels of vertical space.
              const SizedBox(height: 10),


              // Row arranges its children horizontally.
              Row(

                // Distributes the children evenly across the Row.
                mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceEvenly,

                // Widgets inside the Row.
                children: [

                  // First Container.
                  Container(
                    width: 70,
                    height: 70,
                    color: Colors.red,

                    // Places the letter A in the center.
                    child: const Center(
                      child: Text("A"),
                    ),
                  ),


                  // Second Container.
                  Container(
                    width: 70,
                    height: 70,
                    color: Colors.green,

                    // Places the letter B in the center.
                    child: const Center(
                      child: Text("B"),
                    ),
                  ),


                  // Third Container.
                  Container(
                    width: 70,
                    height: 70,
                    color: Colors.orange,

                    // Places the letter C in the center.
                    child: const Center(
                      child: Text("C"),
                    ),
                  ),
                ],
              ),


              // Adds 30 pixels of vertical space.
              const SizedBox(height: 30),


              // ------------------------------------------------
              // COLUMN EXAMPLE
              // ------------------------------------------------

              // Displays the heading "2. Column Widget".
              const Text(
                "2. Column Widget",

                // Text formatting.
                style: TextStyle(
                  fontSize: 22,
                  fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                ),
              ),


              // Adds 10 pixels of vertical space.
              const SizedBox(height: 10),


              // Column arranges its children vertically.
              Column(
                children: [

                  // First Container.
                  Container(
                    width: 150,
                    height: 50,
                    color: Colors.purple,

                    // Places "First" in the center.
                    child: const Center(
                      child: Text("First"),
                    ),
                  ),


                  // Adds 10 pixels between containers.
                  const SizedBox(height: 10),


                  // Second Container.
                  Container(
                    width: 150,
                    height: 50,
                    color: Colors.teal,

                    // Places "Second" in the center.
                    child: const Center(
                      child: Text("Second"),
                    ),
                  ),


                  // Adds 10 pixels between containers.
                  const SizedBox(height: 10),


                  // Third Container.
                  Container(
                    width: 150,
                    height: 50,
                    color: Colors.amber,

                    // Places "Third" in the center.
                    child: const Center(
                      child: Text("Third"),
                    ),
                  ),
                ],
              ),


              // Adds 30 pixels of vertical space.
              const SizedBox(height: 30),


              // ------------------------------------------------
              // STACK EXAMPLE
              // ------------------------------------------------

              // Displays the heading "3. Stack Widget".
              const Text(
                "3. Stack Widget",

                // Text formatting.
                style: TextStyle(
                  fontSize: 22,
                  fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                ),
              ),


              // Adds 10 pixels of vertical space.
              const SizedBox(height: 10),


              // Centers the Stack on the screen.
              Center(
                child: Stack(

                  // Aligns the children in the center of the Stack.
                  alignment: Alignment.center,

                  // Widgets are placed one on top of another.
                  children: [

                    // Largest blue square.
                    Container(
                      width: 220,
                      height: 220,
                      color: Colors.blue,
                    ),


                    // Green square is placed over the blue square.
                    Container(
                      width: 150,
                      height: 150,
                      color: Colors.green,
                    ),


                    // Red square is placed over the green square.
                    Container(
                      width: 80,
                      height: 80,
                      color: Colors.red,
                    ),


                    // Text is placed over all the containers.
                    const Text(
                      "Stack",

                      // Text formatting.
                      style: TextStyle(
                        color: Colors.white,
                        fontSize: 20,
                        fontWeight: FontWeight.bold,
                      ),
                    ),
                  ],
                ),
              ),
            ],
          ),
        ),
      ),
    );
  }
}


Explanation
Understand the three layouts
1. Row — Horizontal layout
Row(
  children: [
    Text("A"),
    Text("B"),
    Text("C"),
  ],
)

The widgets are arranged left to right:

A       B       C
→       →       →

In your program:

Row(
  mainAxisAlignment: MainAxisAlignment.spaceEvenly,
  children: [
    Container(...),
    Container(...),
    Container(...),
  ],
)

spaceEvenly distributes equal space around the children.

2. Column — Vertical layout
Column(
  children: [
    Text("First"),
    Text("Second"),
    Text("Third"),
  ],
)

The widgets are arranged top to bottom:

First
  ↓
Second
  ↓
Third

Your program uses:

Column(
  children: [
    Container(...),
    SizedBox(height: 10),
    Container(...),
    SizedBox(height: 10),
    Container(...),
  ],
)

SizedBox(height: 10) creates 10 pixels of vertical space.

3. Stack — Overlapping layout

A Stack places widgets on top of each other.

Your program creates:

┌─────────────────────┐
│      BLUE           │
│    ┌───────────┐    │
│    │   GREEN   │    │
│    │   ┌────┐  │    │
│    │   │RED │  │    │
│    │   │Stack│  │    │
│    │   └────┘  │    │
│    └───────────┘    │
└─────────────────────┘

The order is important:

children: [
  Blue,
  Green,
  Red,
  Text("Stack"),
]

The first widget is at the back, and later widgets appear on top.

Important concepts to remember
Widget	Purpose	Direction
Row	Arrange widgets horizontally	→
Column	Arrange widgets vertically	↓
Stack	Place widgets on top of each other	Overlap
Center	Center a widget	Center
Container	Create and style a box	—
SizedBox	Add fixed space	—
Padding	Add space around content	—
SingleChildScrollView	Make content scrollable	—
Simple memory trick
ROW    →  Left to Right

COLUMN ↓  Top to Bottom

STACK  ⬆  One widget over another


